# craft architecture (ADR 030)

## Pure core (hard rule)

- `craft-core` and `craft-proto` must have **no I/O**: no `tokio`, sockets, disk, or wall clock.
- Consensus is `RaftInput → (state, RaftOutput)`; effects are **data**, executed by outer runtime.
- Time in core is **logical ticks** (`RaftNode::tick`), not `Instant::now()`.

## Ports & adapters

| Port | Prod | Test / sim |
|------|------|------------|
| `RaftStorage` | `RedbStorage` | `MemoryStorage` |
| `Transport` | QUIC | `LocalNetwork` |
| `ActorStateStore` | Redis | `InMemoryStore` |

- New port = trait + **≥2 implementations**. One impl → do not abstract yet.
- Adapters depend on core; **never** core → adapter.

## Where code lives

- `craft-core` — pure Raft FSM
- `craft-storage` / `craft-net` — trait + adapters
- `craft-actor` — runtime glue (`RaftDriver`, actors)
- `craft` — public facade (`CraftCluster::builder`)
- `craft-node` — reference binary only

## Anti-patterns

```rust
// ❌ I/O inside craft-core
async fn propose() { transport.send(...).await; }

// ✅ Effects returned; runtime executes
fn propose(&mut self, cmd: Cmd) -> Vec<Output> { vec![Output::SendRpc { .. }] }
```

Do not add `domain/` / `infrastructure/` layering inside crates. Shared wire types in `craft-proto` are intentional.
